1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for Kasuga, floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes fly off too.

3
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:32,860
onto the head of the
carpenter I was choking,

4
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase after some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
Kameari, one yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls toward the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end like this too, won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,740
Katsushika Shibamata,
they say that's happiness.

12
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,420
Only after losing it did I realize.

13
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:24,700
Because I'm such an idiot.

14
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:55,220
It's a bite! Set the hook quick!

15
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:55,640
Yes!

16
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,440
I got one, senpai!

17
00:01:58,440 --> 00:01:59,720
Is this the time to be happy?

18
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:01,440
The line tension is too high.

19
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:02,780
At this rate, it'll snap!

20
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:03,620
What do I do?

21
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:05,900
Loosen the drag and let out some line!

22
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:06,960
The drag button is...

23
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:11,320
Clumsy! The line got cut, you idiot.

24
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,340
Too bad, Honda.

25
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:16,920
That was a big one, too bad.

26
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,040
Naive, naive.

27
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:20,740
The one I caught didn't
fight anywhere near that hard.

28
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:24,360
Speaking of which, senior, you reeled
in a 23-pound monster, didn't you?

29
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,480
Well, well.

30
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,420
Did you say something about fishing?

31
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:30,760
Wh-what n-nothing, nothing at all.

32
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,140
*Jooots*

33
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,200
Y-yes.

34
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,400
What's that you're hiding behind your back?

35
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:38,000
*Jooots*

36
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:41,380
Alright, alright already.

37
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:45,000
Sorry about that.
I was playing a fishing game.

38
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,400
A fishing game?

39
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,400
Didn't you say the Chief also goes fishing?

40
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:52,174
I specialize in crucian carp,

41
00:02:52,224 --> 00:02:55,020
but just the other day I went
and caught a 50-centimeter one.

42
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:57,396
Speaking of which,
when I went to the Chief's house,

43
00:02:57,446 --> 00:02:59,960
there was a fishing rod
that looked expensive.

44
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,620
That's a one-of-a-kind piece
made by a famous craftsman.

45
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:07,440
If the Chief likes fishing, how about joining me?
Shall we go catch some bass?

46
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:10,120
That's a toy, isn't it? I don't do toys.

47
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,700
Chief, you shouldn't look down on it.

48
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:15,320
When you catch something,
it vibrates just like the real thing.

49
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:18,960
Now that you mention it,
it does have a proper reel too.

50
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:22,880
Choosing the bass lake and the lure,

51
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:25,600
the sonar even shows the water
quality and the lure's depth.

52
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,680
It's an excellent gadget
with all those functions.

53
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,400
It's pretty serious, isn't it?

54
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,340
So how does it work?

55
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:32,140
You're getting into it now, Chief!

56
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,700
Which lake should we go to?

57
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:36,980
Let's go with this one.

58
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:38,520
Next is the boat.

59
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,860
You look at the sonar and
aim for where the bass are.

60
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:44,840
The lure's depth also shows up on the side.

61
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,780
What? Then it's easy to catch them!

62
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:48,632
You're being naive.

63
00:03:48,682 --> 00:03:51,840
The most important thing in lure
fishing is choosing the lure.

64
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,004
Weather, water quality,

65
00:03:53,054 --> 00:03:56,720
and the route you take all matter. Without the right lure,
you won't catch any bass.

66
00:03:57,180 --> 00:03:57,480
I see.

67
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:01,780
For beginners, the Spider Jig in brown is
a safe bet since the bass bite on it well.

68
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:03,440
Then I'll go with that.

69
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,140
Alright, go ahead and start casting.

70
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,220
Here it comes!

71
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,840
It's got some serious strength!

72
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:27,980
This one must be a real monster.

73
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:32,960
Got it! I landed it!

74
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:38,860
W-wow!

75
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:41,720
It's a giant 25-pound bass!

76
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:42,860
Amazing, for a first timer!

77
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:43,620
Is that so?

78
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:47,580
I'm known as a fishing genius, you know.

79
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:51,000
What's your personal best, in pounds?

80
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:54,340
I forgot... how many pounds was it again?

81
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:57,000
But you said it was 23 pounds!

82
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,720
What, 23 pounds?

83
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:02,300
You, who does nothing but play games,
caught 23 pounds?

84
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,880
And I, a first-timer, caught 25 pounds.
Go figure.

85
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,320
What's with that smug grin?

86
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:10,920
Getting cocky just because
you caught one by luck!

87
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:12,480
Let me see it, please.

88
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:15,300
I'll catch an even bigger bass than that!

89
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:20,740
Get the boat closer to the rocks!

90
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,900
Yes!

91
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:41,900
Great pull! This has to be a big one!

92
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:45,280
What's wrong? For a big one,
the pull's pretty weak, isn't it?

93
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,863
That's why amateurs are such a pain.

94
00:05:46,913 --> 00:05:49,771
The 100-battle-hardened
big bass pretends to be weak,

95
00:05:49,821 --> 00:05:53,400
then thrashes wildly just before
it's reeled in and snaps the line.

96
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,540
I went and caught one.

97
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:58,240
It's just a bluegill, a trash fish.

98
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:02,560
Let's see, so what does it weigh?
Five pounds.

99
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,246
Heh heh heh.
After all, when it comes to fishing,

100
00:06:05,296 --> 00:06:07,480
even at games, you can't beat me.

101
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:11,173
Well, ever since I was a kid, from
crucian carp fishing to Christmas fishing,

102
00:06:11,223 --> 00:06:13,420
I've never lost to anyone at fishing.

103
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:15,860
Tree, you say?

104
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,800
I hooked "fishing" with another "fishing."

105
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,700
Dad jokes, pure dad jokes.

106
00:06:20,110 --> 00:06:23,240
Well, Ryotsu-kun, that's the kind
of talent that counts, isn't it?

107
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,280
No matter how hard you try,

108
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:27,520
you'll never beat me, you know.

109
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,020
Mmmmm.

110
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:31,240
Well, I suppose that's just life.

111
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:31,820
Mmmm.

112
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:33,540
Hmph, you just wait.

113
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:37,620
Hey, where do you think you're going?
You're on duty!

114
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:41,040
Judging by how he looked,
I don't think he'll be back anytime soon.

115
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,820
It's the Chief's fault.

116
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:45,000
Because you hurt Ryo-chan's pride.

117
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,800
Well, I got a little carried away.

118
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:51,500
Knowing Ryo-chan, he's surely
plotting some outrageous revenge.

119
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:55,100
The weather's looking suspicious, so

120
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,180
I'm going to head home now,
if you don't mind.

121
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:57,960
Excuse me.

122
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,700
Senpai's sure taking his time coming back

123
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:09,420
He's probably drowning his
sorrows somewhere, I bet.

124
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:11,340
Who's drowning their sorrows, you say?

125
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:15,200
Ryotsu

126
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:17,080
Where did you go, senpai?

127
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,960
I just ran over to an
acquaintance's toy shop.

128
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:20,940
Toy shop?

129
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:23,000
Yeah, to pick up this thing.

130
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,960
Chief, let's go another round with this!

131
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,700
What, Bass Fishers again?

132
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,480
This isn't Bass Fishers.

133
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:34,460
It's the new game console from the series,
Gal Fishers.

134
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,380
Gal Fishers.

135
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:41,140
It's a game where you catch
gals instead of black bass.

136
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:46,480
You idiot! Slacking off on duty
and borrowing that worthless junk!

137
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:50,920
I don't care what you say!
Come on, let's see who can catch more gals!

138
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,900
How ridiculous!
I'm not playing such a stupid game!

139
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,920
Let me see, these documents...

140
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,260
So you're running away.

141
00:07:58,500 --> 00:07:59,480
Ugh, n-no, I'm not!

142
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:03,980
I'm saying I won't go along with an
outrageous game like catching gals!

143
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:07,880
You said you'd never lost at fishing,
but that was a lie, wasn't it?

144
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:14,860
That 23-pound bass was probably
just a fluke catch too, right?

145
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:17,340
Bug a bug, bug bug.

146
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:22,180
Working under a big-mouthed coward of a boss is so annoying,
honestly.

147
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:24,140
He really isn't a man, that one.

148
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:26,940
Does he even have two balls,
or is he just wishy-washy?

149
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:30,080
Even after all this,
refusing to face me is just hopeless.

150
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,180
This is unbearable, I can't take it anymore.

151
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,720
Shut up, Atsu.

152
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:37,120
Alright, fine, if you're going to push me that far,
I'll take you on.

153
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:38,340
Why, it's the Chief!

154
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:39,020
Chief!

155
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:42,060
Just as expected of the Chief!
You really are a man!

156
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,200
Teach me how to catch them, Ryotsu!

157
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:47,180
The way you fish is pretty
much the same as Bass Fishers,

158
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:51,180
but this one has a digital camera,
so you can catch real gals.

159
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:53,440
Well, let me give it a try, so please watch.

160
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:57,560
I've got a bite already!

161
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,682
Instead of a fish finder,
this game console has

162
00:09:00,732 --> 00:09:02,700
a gal detector built in.

163
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:07,120
And it responds to real, living women.

164
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:14,940
Not bad, these are some cute gals!

165
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:24,180
Next, we pick a lake where
they're likely to hang out.

166
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:26,240
That's not a lake, is it?

167
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:29,380
Our catch isn't bass, it's gals, after all.

168
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:32,360
Well, girls these days are all ko-gals, so

169
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,660
set it to Harajuku.

170
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:38,020
Next, instead of a boat,

171
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:39,440
we choose a car?

172
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:42,900
She has short hair and looks lively,
so she's the outdoorsy type.

173
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:45,200
In a four-wheel-drive Range Rover.

174
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:47,260
As expected, Senpai, your read is sharp.

175
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:49,840
Now, what should the lure be?

176
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:51,680
The lures are quite different, too.

177
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:53,360
Well, they're practical, aren't they?

178
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:57,020
The lure chooses what the gal
would like to receive as a present.

179
00:09:57,020 --> 00:10:00,760
Well, she's a high schooler,
so a Tiffany ring is about right.

180
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:02,600
Alright, setup complete.

181
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:04,880
Alright!

182
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,000
Go!

183
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:15,340
A bite!

184
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:17,320
Perfect opening!

185
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,200
Alright, keep pulling it in!

186
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:22,540
I got it! I caught one!

187
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:24,980
Eek! Look at her! Eek! Look at her!

188
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,140
Look, look, look!

189
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:29,880
What's this? It's like a photo sticker.

190
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:33,380
When you reel one in, a photo of a gal appears,
just like a photo sticker.

191
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:39,700
And the built-in computer compares her to your
ideal face and figure and calculates a beauty score.

192
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:45,000
And gals scoring 70 or higher in
beauty come out in swimsuits as a bonus.

193
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,740
That's quite the niche, elaborate design.

194
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:48,920
Chief, did you figure out how to use it?

195
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:49,360
Yeah.

196
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:53,360
But just competing against each
other isn't very exciting, is it?

197
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:58,080
I know! How about we each wager our most precious treasure?
What do you say?

198
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:58,420
What?

199
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:00,640
I'll wager this.

200
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:02,140
I don't want that junk.

201
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:04,240
This thing cost 350,000 yen, you know.

202
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:06,620
I don't have any treasures that expensive.

203
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:07,920
Sure you do.

204
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,800
That crucian carp rod of yours.

205
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:11,360
No, not that one.

206
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:14,000
Then let's make you admit defeat.

207
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,660
Get down on your knees
and kowtow in front of me

208
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:18,320
and promise you'll never
brag about fishing again.

209
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:20,020
Have you bow your head, shall we?

210
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,000
What?

211
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,540
You don't wanna bet because
you're not confident you'll win

212
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:26,060
What's it going to be?

213
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,640
Grovel or face the challenge?

214
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:28,800
Which will it be?

215
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:29,780
Fine, I get it.

216
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,940
Let's settle this with the rod on the line.

217
00:11:31,940 --> 00:11:33,300
Chief.

218
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:35,500
How do we decide the winner?

219
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:36,080
Well then,

220
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:40,820
whoever scores more points
within one hour wins.

221
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:42,660
Fine, that works.

222
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:44,260
Then get in position.

223
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:47,940
Ready, set, go!

224
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,960
Fast forward

225
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:30,640
It's Komachi-kun.

226
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:35,660
Komachi-kun said she often
goes shopping in Ueno, right?

227
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:38,340
So I set her habitat to Ueno.

228
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:41,220
Komachi-kun looks like
a mini-gal on the outside,

229
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:43,340
but she's surprisingly old-fashioned.

230
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,880
The car is this one, and the lure is this.

231
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:47,140
Ready, set,

232
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:05,860
Miss, how about we go grab some
kombu tea near Togenuki Jizo, mister?

233
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:07,100
Lame~

234
00:13:07,540 --> 00:13:11,080
If you go on a date with me,
I'll buy you clothes from Building Search.

235
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:15,240
You're my type, mister.
I'll go on a date with you!

236
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:23,440
Got one! I reeled it in!

237
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:29,920
30 points? I thought it would be higher.

238
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:33,400
Komachi types are about that level,
you know.

239
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,380
Alright, now it's my turn.

240
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:39,040
Ready, set, go!

241
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:53,640
Yeah, I'll take her for
a drive in my Porsche.

242
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,780
Sorry, but gin and tonic, though.

243
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:59,080
If she goes for a drive,
I'll give her a present.

244
00:13:59,980 --> 00:14:02,386
Not serious,

245
00:14:02,436 --> 00:14:04,000
I'll go for a drive.

246
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,120
Fish on!

247
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:10,420
This feels like a sure 90 points.

248
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:12,720
Either one's fine, whatever.

249
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:15,340
How about a suit from your in-house brand?

250
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:17,060
Let's go!

251
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,900
Naoko, I'm coming, I'm coming!

252
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:19,560
Alright.

253
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:26,800
Yes, I caught one!

254
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:29,480
Naoko's probably under 50 points anyway.

255
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,180
Yes, 70 points!

256
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:35,632
What? That Naoko got 70 points?

257
00:14:35,682 --> 00:14:38,620
What kind of taste does
whoever made this game have?

258
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,420
Damn it, mine's the same too!

259
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:46,260
Yes! Come on out, 100 points!

260
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,477
25 points. Why the hell is it 25 points?

261
00:14:50,527 --> 00:14:52,840
Nothing I can do. This bastard, you chicken.

262
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:55,700
What's your problem?
Just let it slide a little, won't you?

263
00:14:56,380 --> 00:14:58,400
But a violation is a violation, you know.

264
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,960
What the hell is that attitude of yours,
you bastard?

265
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:04,840
Damn, she's so ugly.

266
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,360
What did you say?!

267
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:09,600
Sorry for being ugly

268
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:13,380
Speaking of which, what about you,
you ass-faced bastard!

269
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:18,640
I'll accept the 25 points, then.

270
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:20,660
Let's change the points, Ryotsu.

271
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:37,860
Not catching anything at all.

272
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,320
How's Uocho doing?

273
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,560
What is it?

274
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:44,940
Ryotsu, I'm heading to the station.

275
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,980
Rather than catching gals
whose background you don't know,

276
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:49,400
it's easier to catch parents
you have some idea about.

277
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:52,420
Besides, there's a parents' meeting today.

278
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:56,000
Hey, who's getting ahead all on their own!

279
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:59,300
Wait up, I'm coming too!

280
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:23,300
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

281
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:26,060
I just caught every parent
attending the meeting.

282
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:28,520
Maybe I'm a real gal-killer

283
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,640
Don't make me laugh.

284
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:34,080
They're all old hags, aren't they?

285
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,200
Say whatever you want.

286
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:37,000
Anyway, the only one you caught

287
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,000
was a 25-point girl, wasn't it?

288
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:41,880
Unlike you, Chief,
I don't need to catch big fish to win.

289
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:44,080
If I catch two more,
I'll turn this around in no time.

290
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:46,780
That one there

291
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:50,340
A spirited girl,
a boy-crazy one, the Saotome type.

292
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,040
Alright, I'm taking her!

293
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:54,460
I'm reeling her in myself.

294
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:56,140
Chief, that's my catch, isn't it?

295
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:58,380
First come, first served, right, Ryotsu?

296
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:04,040
Well, in this game's battle mode, if we both target the same catch,
the one who hooks it first should get the points.

297
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:05,960
Not confident, Ryotsu-kun?

298
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:08,740
What? I'll absolutely reel her in first,
just watch!

299
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:11,380
Let's use a powerful bass bait lure.

300
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:12,620
What's this bass bait thing?

301
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:17,540
It's a lure with a spinning disc that makes
noise on the water's surface to excite the fish.

302
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:19,400
Well, you could call
it the background music.

303
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,860
Alright, go on! Go!

304
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:35,540
Miss, why don't you come with
me all the way to Daikoku Pier?

305
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:38,340
No, no, miss.
Come with me all the way to Odaiba.

306
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,860
Well, let me think. What should I do?

307
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:43,920
Allow me to give you this Bulgari watch.

308
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:46,320
And this is a Cartier ring.

309
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:51,760
And how about a drive while
listening to the new Sharanpy song?

310
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:56,460
I love Sharanpy!
I'll go for a drive, for sure!

311
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,660
Fish arm!

312
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:03,000
The background music did the talking,
didn't it?

313
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:09,860
That's pulling up nicely, Saotome.
Adjusting the line tension is tricky.

314
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:13,040
Snap off, snap off!
If it gets away, I'll take it!

315
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:14,200
Damn it!

316
00:18:14,740 --> 00:18:15,600
Yes!

317
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:18,480
Look, 85 points!

318
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:21,360
Hehe, how about that!

319
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:23,080
Phew, I'm not losing.

320
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:24,160
Hey, wait, you little -

321
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:29,600
Oh, it's Reiko-kun!

322
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:31,320
If it's her,
she's definitely going to get a high score.

323
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:34,860
Yeah, if it's Reiko,
she might even get a perfect 100.

324
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:36,290
Alright,

325
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:39,860
if I reel this one in,
I'll widen the gap all at once.

326
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:43,820
Don't be naive. The higher the beauty rating,
the harder the conditions get.

327
00:18:43,820 --> 00:18:46,520
The weather's rainy,
so the water's gotten murky too.

328
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:50,840
Don't worry, Reiko is super rich, so luxury
cars and brand names won't work on her.

329
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,140
Keeping it simple is the surest way to go.

330
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:55,060
I wonder if it'll really go that smoothly.

331
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:57,160
Alright.

332
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:57,960
Go for it!

333
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:18,940
Yo, Reiko!
Rough day in the rain Wanna hop in?

334
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:21,000
I don't know what to do...

335
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:26,760
Reiko-kun! How about joining me for a meal,
if you're free?

336
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:28,960
Not a Mini Cooper? How cute!

337
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:32,080
The Chief's so stylish, isn't he?
Reiko's getting in!

338
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:41,400
I'm such a sucker for
simple gifts like this.

339
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:44,640
So, where should we eat?
What do you feel like having?

340
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:47,240
Maybe French food?

341
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,240
French food

342
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:50,480
The restaurant's in Paris...

343
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:51,200
Paris

344
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:56,220
Just for a meal,
you'd go all the way to France?

345
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:59,980
French food really is best enjoyed in France,
after all.

346
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:02,180
W-what's this incredible lure!

347
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:04,940
The line keeps running out!
She's not coming in at all!

348
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:08,740
A big catch like Reiko's class
won't be reeled in that easily, boss!

349
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:10,460
That one!

350
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:13,460
Maria!

351
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:17,220
Maria should be just as good as Reiko.

352
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:21,100
I know everything about her,
so I can win her over easily.

353
00:20:21,300 --> 00:20:22,940
I won't let you widen the gap!

354
00:20:23,340 --> 00:20:24,140
Hyaah!

355
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:26,200
Go on!

356
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:31,980
Maria!

357
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:34,320
Ryo-sama!

358
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:43,160
Maria, would you like some of these?

359
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:45,820
They're my homemade cookies.

360
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:47,480
Maria, how wonderful!

361
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:50,060
Bzzt!

362
00:20:53,180 --> 00:20:54,880
Maria's totally smitten with me.

363
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:57,180
Reeling her in is a piece of cake.

364
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:17,720
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

365
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:20,480
What? Minus 100 points?

366
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:24,580
This game machine sees right through Maria.
It knows he's a man!

367
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:27,540
Ha ha you've dug your own grave, Ryotsu.

368
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:30,380
Well, that radio-controlled
helicopter is mine, then.

369
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:32,260
Eeh, just you watch.

370
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:36,460
Come on, come on,
step right up and have a bite!

371
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:38,580
It's all free of charge.

372
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:39,060
Yay!

373
00:21:39,060 --> 00:21:40,920
For a gorilla, you're pretty thoughtful.

374
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:42,500
Give me some too.

375
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:43,360
Give me some too.

376
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:44,200
This is amazing.

377
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:44,900
Ugh.

378
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:45,300
Ugh.

379
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:45,660
Ugh.

380
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:46,120
Ugh.

381
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:47,180
What do you think you're doing?

382
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,500
I'm the one who scattered the bait.

383
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:51,180
These are all my fish. Go find your own.

384
00:21:51,540 --> 00:21:52,560
Well, go on, go on.

385
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:07,140
Phew, they're biting left and right!

386
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:10,920
Uh-oh, at this rate I'm
going to be overtaken.

387
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:13,280
Wow, that's amazing, 100 points in one go!

388
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:13,980
What?

389
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,640
Nice-bodied gal!

390
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:21,580
Yes! Got her!

391
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:24,460
That's dirty, Ryotsu! That catch is mine!

392
00:22:24,460 --> 00:22:26,120
Dirty or not, there's no such thing
as cheating in a contest, is there?

393
00:22:26,460 --> 00:22:27,500
Got one!

394
00:22:27,860 --> 00:22:28,600
Yay!

395
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:33,500
Why am I at minus 50 points?

396
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:35,640
No way!

397
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:42,300
What?

398
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:43,400
What is it?

399
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:46,000
No, it's nothing.

400
00:22:46,620 --> 00:22:48,000
What's your problem, you!

401
00:22:48,580 --> 00:22:49,280
Murder!

402
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:57,320
Only three minutes left.
At this rate, I'll lose.

403
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,220
A carpenter found it!

404
00:23:00,940 --> 00:23:02,100
Alright, let's head back.

405
00:23:15,740 --> 00:23:16,460
This is

406
00:23:21,520 --> 00:23:22,740
You idiot!

407
00:23:23,380 --> 00:23:26,760
What do you mean, getting so absorbed in the
game that you peek into the women's changing room?

408
00:23:27,180 --> 00:23:29,060
I'm really sorry.

409
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:31,020
It's a written reprimand!
Put your heart into it!

410
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:35,880
We got lucky it ended with just a written reprimand,
didn't we?

411
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:38,312
Silence! I've served in the
police for over thirty years,

412
00:23:38,362 --> 00:23:41,720
and now I've been forced to
write my first written reprimand!

413
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:48,060
H-he's a tough one, this guy.

414
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:48,800
Mayor!

415
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:51,160
No, this is, well, that's...

416
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:52,040
Chief.

417
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,380
Shall we go?

418
00:23:53,620 --> 00:23:54,640
Want to go at it?

419
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:57,500
Hey, what do you think
you're doing yourself!

420
00:23:57,980 --> 00:23:58,880
Let's take advantage of the opening!

421
00:23:59,140 --> 00:24:00,480
Okay, okay, okay, forgive me!

422
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:05,800
I see, I see.

423
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:08,060
The old man sure went through a lot

424
00:24:08,060 --> 00:24:09,500
It's all lies

425
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:11,500
What an outrageous old geezer.

426
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:15,260
He's been a habitual con artist since the
Katsushika police station was first built.

427
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:18,600
Hey, you dumped that troublesome old geezer on me,
didn't you?

428
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:22,180
Next time, the old man and the bomber,
see you then.

429
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:37,160
People say I'm a woman
who can't fall in love,

430
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:42,760
but I have so many things I want to do.

431
00:24:44,740 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

432
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:58,940
I want to be freer than a bird.

433
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:07,140
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

434
00:25:09,120 --> 00:25:15,260
My heart's longing, sorry, wait for me.

435
00:25:15,260 --> 00:25:22,200
The future in a panorama,
a dazzling time-lapse.

436
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:26,520
You understand, right?

437
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:30,040
Sorry, wait for me.

